.Dd July 26, 2026
.Dt RACOON 8
.Os
.\"
.Sh NAME
.Nm racoon
.Nd IKE (ISAKMP/Oakley) key management daemon
.\"
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm racoon
.Bk -words
.Op Fl 46BdFLtVv
.Ek
.Bk -words
.Op Fl f Ar configfile
.Ek
.Bk -words
.Op Fl l Ar logfile
.Ek
.Bk -words
.Op Fl P Ar isakmp-natt-port
.Ek
.Bk -words
.Op Fl p Ar isakmp-port
.Ek
.\"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
speaks the IKE
.Pq ISAKMP/Oakley
key management protocol,
to establish security associations with other hosts.
The SPD
.Pq Security Policy Database
in the kernel usually triggers
.Nm .
.Nm
usually sends all informational messages, warnings and error messages to
.Xr syslogd 8
with the facility
.Dv LOG_DAEMON
and the priority
.Dv LOG_INFO .
Debugging messages are sent with the priority
.Dv LOG_DEBUG .
You should configure
.Xr syslog.conf 5
appropriately to see these messages.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl 4
.It Fl 6
Specify the default address family for the sockets.
.It Fl B
Install SA(s) from the file which is specified in
.Xr racoon.conf 5 .
.It Fl d
Increase the debug level.
Multiple
.Fl d
arguments will increase the debug level even more.
.It Fl F
Run
.Nm
in the foreground.
Log lines are always written to
.Va stdout
.Pq line-buffered, so a line appears as soon as it is complete,
rather than whenever the platform's default stdio buffering next
flushes
.Em in addition to
their normal destination, which remains
.Xr syslogd 8
unless
.Fl l
selects a log file instead.
This is intentional:
.Fl F
is meant for interactive debugging at a terminal, where an operator
watching
.Va stdout
still wants the same lines syslog would otherwise carry.
Under a service manager whose default configuration captures a unit's
.Va stdout
into the same log store its
.Xr syslogd 8
compatibility socket also feeds
.Po
e.g. systemd, where
.Xr journald 8
commonly does both
.Pc ,
this shows up as every line appearing twice in
.Xr journalctl 1 .
Pick one destination if that is undesired: either pass
.Fl l
.Ar logfile
to stop the
.Xr syslogd 8
half
.Po
.Va stdout
still carries the same lines
.Pc ,
or configure the service manager to discard
.Nm Ns 's
.Va stdout
.Po
e.g. systemd's
.Cm StandardOutput=null
.Pc
and keep only the syslog/journal copy.
.It Fl f Ar configfile
Use
.Ar configfile
as the configuration file instead of the default.
.It Fl L
Include
.Ar file_name:line_number:function_name
in all messages.
.It Fl l Ar logfile
Use
.Ar logfile
as the logging file instead of
.Xr syslogd 8 .
.It Fl P Ar isakmp-natt-port
Use
.Ar isakmp-natt-port
for NAT-Traversal port-floating.
The default is 4500.
.It Fl p Ar isakmp-port
Listen to the ISAKMP key exchange on port
.Ar isakmp-port
instead of the default port number, 500.
.It Fl t
Check the configuration file specified by
.Fl f
.Pq or the default, if none is given
for syntax errors, then exit.
.Nm
performs the same initialization and parsing it would at normal
startup, including asking the kernel which algorithms it supports,
but does not open the ISAKMP or admin sockets, write a pid file, or
become a daemon.
This requires the same privileges as running
.Nm
normally.
.It Fl V
Print racoon version and compilation options and exit.
.It Fl v
This flag causes the packet dump be more verbose, with higher
debugging level.
.El
.Pp
.Nm
assumes the presence of the kernel random number device
.Xr rnd 4
at
.Pa /dev/urandom .
.\"
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The command exits with 0 on success, and non-zero on errors.
With
.Fl t ,
it exits with 0 if the configuration file is valid and 1 otherwise,
without starting the daemon either way.
.\"
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /etc/racoon/scripts -compact
.It Pa /etc/racoon.conf
default configuration file.
.It Pa /etc/racoon/scripts
the split-DNS/routing
.Ic phase1_up Ns / Ns Ic phase1_down
scripts (also called hooks) shipped with this project and their
configuration file,
.Pa hooks.conf ,
with packaging defaults; see the Admin Guide
.Pq Pa doc/admin/split-dns.html
in the project source.
.El
.\"
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ipsec 4 ,
.Xr racoon.conf 5 ,
.Xr syslog.conf 5 ,
.Xr racoon-dns-detect 8 ,
.Xr setkey 8 ,
.Xr syslogd 8
.\"
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
command first appeared in the
.Dq YIPS
Yokogawa IPsec implementation.
.\"
.Sh SECURITY CONSIDERATIONS
The use of IKE phase 1 aggressive mode is not recommended,
as described in
.Pa http://www.kb.cert.org/vuls/id/886601 .
